WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.236
-The Trump administration
has announced a new rule

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.870
that would limit
legal immigration

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.306
by imposing a wealth test.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.241
For more on this it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.777 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.845
♪♪

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:15.814
Trump has many racist conspiracy
theories about immigrants.

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:18.118
He thinks they're being
funded by shadowy groups.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.186
He thinks it's a plot
to invade America

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.055
and he's pretty sure
at least one of his sons

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.656
snuck in from Transylvania.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.258
[ Laughter ]
[as Trump] Secret Service,

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.759
he's out of his coffin again.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.527
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:30.963
Trump also has his insane
theory that other countries

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:33.399
are somehow rigging
the visa lottery system,

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.502
to put their worst people
in the lottery.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.036
He's repeated it many times,

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.805
including at a rally
earlier this month.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.706
-How about the lottery system?

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:42.541
[ Booing ]

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:43.910
How about lotteries?

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.679
You put the name in a basket.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.115
The country puts the name
in the basket

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.351
and you pick people
out of the lottery.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.419
Well, let's see,
"This one's a murderer.

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:57.390
[ Laughter ]
This one robbed four banks.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.092
This one, I'd better not say.

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.594
This one,
another murderer."

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.163
Ladies and gentlemen,
another murderer.

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.932
-It sounds like
he's picking his cabinet.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.501
[ Laughter ]
[as Trump] Bank robber.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.202
[ Cheering and applause ]
Oh, a murderer.

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:12.638
Oh, oh, you guys.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:15.975
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.011
You guys, we got a cannibal.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.479
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.313
[ Applause ]

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:23.349
But, Trump continued.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.884
-Think of this:

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.852
Do you think they're gonna
put their great citizens?

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.154
They have great citizens.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.888
They have great people,
like we have great people.

00:01:29.888 --> 00:01:32.692
Do you think those people are
going into a lottery?

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.594
No. And then, we get
these people coming in.

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:36.896
You just take a look.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.465
Look at the people they put
into these lotteries.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.333
-That's not how it works.

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:43.870
Countries don't put people
in the lotteries.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.971
[ Laughter ]
People enter themselves

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:47.574
and it's not murderers, saying,

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.874
"The police are closing in!

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:51.611
I better make my escape,
by entering a random drawing."

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.214
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.916
This is one of Trump's favorite
insane conspiracy theories

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.752
and he's repeated it countless
times throughout his presidency.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.020
-They have a lottery.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.489
You pick people.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:06.993
You think the country's
givin' us their best people?

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.128
No. Visa lottery!

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.530
Visa lottery!

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.766
Boom. Who is this?!
Who is this?

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.903
And then, when they turn out
to be not so good,

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.137
we say, "I wonder why."

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.939
Well, maybe the country's
giving us

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.406
their worst in those lotteries.

00:02:21.406 --> 00:02:22.975
Does that make any sense?

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.044
Think of it: A lottery!

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.078
You pick people.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:27.813
Now, let me ask you.

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:30.249
So, these countries that are
sending people in.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.585
Do you think they're
sending us their finest?

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.087
And then, we wonder why
we have problems.

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:37.222
We're not going to be

00:02:37.222 --> 00:02:39.992
a stupid country anymore!

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:42.595
-Anh, we're still very much
the stupid country.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.297
[ Laughter and applause ]
Stupid is our brand.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:47.867
Obama made us cool.
You made us stupid.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.068
One of the other
problems here is,

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.203
unlike more complicated terms,

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:53.138
Trump thinks he knows
what a lottery is,

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:55.975
so, even though he's wrong,
he's trying to flex his muscles.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.710
I'm surprised he didn't
just start talking

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.478
about scratch-offs,
at some point.

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:01.314
[as Trump]
And they give you a card

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.783
and you use a dime, ideally.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.017
Worst case, your thumb,

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:06.852
and you just start scratching
and, if you get

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:09.388
three matching flags,
that's your new home.

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:11.557
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:15.027
That's how it works
in a [bellowing] lottery!

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:16.796
A visa lottery.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.231
[ Applause ]

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:21.467
Trump feeds his supporters
these racist conspiracy theories

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.636
to make them think
that undeserving immigrants

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.105
are coming here and draining
our public resources,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.440
which is a bigoted lie.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.875
And, now, he's taking that lie
one step further,

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:33.145
by implementing a new rule
that will basically institute

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:36.248
a wealth test, in order
to limit legal immigration.

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:38.985
-A major policy change
by the Trump administration

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:43.056
is trying to dramatically limit
legal immigration into the U.S.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.423
The so-called public charge rule

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:46.525
would make it more difficult
for people who are, again,

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:49.828
here legally, but rely on some
form of government assistance.

00:03:49.828 --> 00:03:53.065
Medicaid, food stamps, housing
vouchers, some of the examples.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:55.501
It would make it harder
for them to get a green card.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.536
The new criteria
favors wealthier,

00:03:57.536 --> 00:03:59.271
more educated immigrants.

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:01.674
The National Immigration
Law Center calls the new rule

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.943
a wealth test on immigrants.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.177
[ Rotors whirring ]
-I don't think it's fair to have

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:07.447
the American taxpayer pay

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:10.049
for people to come
into the United States.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:13.052
I'm tired of seeing our taxpayer

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.321
paying for people
to come into the country

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:19.025
and immediately go onto welfare
and various other things,

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.626
so I think we're doing it right.

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:22.661
-So, now,
you're suddenly concerned

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:24.296
about wasting taxpayers' money?

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.632
You've already spent more
than $100 million,

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:28.200
just on golf trips.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.603
[ Laughter ]
And I have one very simple
fix for this.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.372
We don't need to stop
paying for his golf.

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.740
We just need to stop paying
for his golf cart

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.810
because just imagine how fast
he would lose interest

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.378
if he had to walk.
[as Trump] This sucks.

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:42.315
[ Laughter ]
I'm gonna play a sport

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.816
where you don't have
to move so much,

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.183
like grass luge.

00:04:45.183 --> 00:04:48.120
[ Laughter and clapping ]

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.523
This is fundamentally
antithetical

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.658
to everything that America's
supposed to stand for.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.493
In fact, that ethos
is famously etched

00:04:54.493 --> 00:04:55.828
on the Statue of Liberty

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.230
in the Emma Lazarus poem
"The New Colossus."

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.565
Yesterday,
Trump's acting director

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.567
of U.S. Citizenship
and Immigration Services,

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.235
Ken Cuccinelli,
was asked on NPR

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:04.604
about that poem and said this.

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:06.972
-Would you also agree
that Emma Lazarus's words,

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:10.476
etched on the Statue of Liberty,
"Give me your tired, your poor,"

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:13.145
are also part
of the American ethos?

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:14.413
-They certainly are.

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:15.848
"Give me your tired
and your poor"

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.450
who can stand
on their own two feet

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.885
[ Laughter ]
and who will not become

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.353
a public charge.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.989
-First of all, you can't
just rewrite the poem!

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.825
[ Laughter ]
Especially a poem on a plaque.

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:28.027
Once it's on a plaque,
it's the thing.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.162
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.662
The sign says "No smoking,"

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:32.765
not "No smoking,
but also smoking."

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.201
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:37.837
Second, you want them
to stand on their own two feet?

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.705
Trump can't stand
on his two feet.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:41.607
[ Laughter ]
Look at him.
He's like a drunk guy,

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.843
tryin' real hard
to pretend he's sober.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.245
[ Clapping ]
Trump is doing this

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.347
for two reasons:
one, he's a racist

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:50.649
and racism is at the core
of his immigration policy.

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:53.552
And two, he can't deliver
on any of the other promises

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:54.720
he's made to voters.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.223
That's why his administration
inflicts cruelty

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.857
on desperate migrant families,

00:05:58.857 --> 00:06:01.560
like when they conducted
the largest single-state

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.496
immigration raid
in history last week

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.830
and separated children
from their parents.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.732
Meanwhile, he can't
actually do anything

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:08.867
to help the people
he promised to help:

00:06:08.867 --> 00:06:11.371
the so-called forgotten
men and women of America,

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.473
the working class
he claimed he championed.

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.908
He told them he'd fix everything
and that it would be so easy.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.176
You know, like healthcare.

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.278
-We're gonna get you
something so good.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:22.482
So much less expensive,
so much better.

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:24.716
You know what it's called?
It's better and less expensive.

00:06:24.716 --> 00:06:26.252
That's a good combination.

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:29.489
You're going to have
such great healthcare,

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:34.193
at a tiny fraction of the cost,
and it's gonna be so easy.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.462
-As a general rule,
never take advice from a guy

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:38.631
in a camouflage hat
with orange font because...

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:40.599
[ Laughter ]
it's a weird choice.

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:43.302
I mean, I get the orange,
but not the words, you know?

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:45.238
You've never seen a hunter
going into the woods

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:47.539
in camo gear with bright
orange writing that says,

00:06:47.539 --> 00:06:50.109
"I am a hunter."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:51.444
Now, a universal
healthcare system

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:53.913
that guarantees healthcare
as a human right

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:56.315
is possible,
as many industrialized nations

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.383
and Democrats running
for president have shown,

00:06:58.383 --> 00:07:00.185
but Trump made the promise

00:07:00.185 --> 00:07:02.755
without having any clue
what he was talking about

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:04.256
and then, of course,
once it came time

00:07:04.256 --> 00:07:06.058
to come up with an actual plan,

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:09.127
like any con artist,
he tried to talk in circles

00:07:09.127 --> 00:07:10.963
until people forgot
what he'd promised.

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.899
This will be a plan where
you can choose your doctor.

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:16.702
This will be a plan
where you can choose your plan.

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.371
-[Chuckling]
-And you know what the plan is?

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:20.939
This is the plan.
-Oh my God.

00:07:20.939 --> 00:07:22.641
He always sounds like
he's playing Taboo

00:07:22.641 --> 00:07:25.878
and he can't think
of a second clue

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:26.946
that's not [indistinct]

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:28.714
[as Trump]
Uh, it's a plan, you know.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.582
Like a plan. A plan.
It's a plan.

00:07:30.582 --> 00:07:33.285
You know, a plan!
[ Buzzer ]

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:34.986
The word was plan.
I was cheating.

00:07:34.986 --> 00:07:37.556
[ Laughter and clapping ]

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:40.226
I was cheating the whole time.

00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:43.029
Then, there was Trump's promise
to save manufacturing jobs.

00:07:43.029 --> 00:07:44.897
During a stop in Ohio
two years ago,

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.832
he told residents
he would singlehandedly

00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:49.468
save their manufacturing plants.

00:07:49.468 --> 00:07:52.238
In fact, he literally told
the people at his rally

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:55.074
who were worried about losing
their jobs not to move.

00:07:55.074 --> 00:07:58.477
-I rode through your
beautiful roads,

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:01.813
coming up from the airport
and I was --

00:08:01.813 --> 00:08:06.251
I was lookin' at some
of those big, once incredible,

00:08:06.251 --> 00:08:08.353
job-producing factories.

00:08:08.353 --> 00:08:12.391
And my wife, Melania, said,
"What happened?"

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:17.229
I said, "Those jobs
have left Ohio."

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:19.131
They're all
comin' back.

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:20.733
[ Cheering and applause ]
They're all comin' back.

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:22.435
[ Whistling ]
Comin' back.

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:25.037
[ Applause ]

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:26.905
Don't move.

00:08:26.905 --> 00:08:29.942
Don't sell your house.
Don't sell your house.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:32.911
-If Donald Trump, a man
who has gone bankrupt six times

00:08:32.911 --> 00:08:34.446
and is infamous
for some of the biggest

00:08:34.446 --> 00:08:36.148
real estate disasters
in history,

00:08:36.148 --> 00:08:38.350
tells you don't sell your
house, sell your house.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:41.420
[ Laughter and applause ]
Trump is --

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.589
Trump is the kind of guy
who would tell people,

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:44.857
during a tornado,

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.658
[as Trump] "You definitely
wanna be by a window.

00:08:46.658 --> 00:08:48.560
[ Laughter ]
Be by a window,

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.962
so you can see it.
Sometimes they have cows inside.

00:08:50.962 --> 00:08:52.464
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:55.201
Once again, you'll
never guess what happened.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.469
A plant nearby, in Lordstown,
closed in March.

00:08:57.469 --> 00:09:00.305
Then, when the cruel reality
of Trump's empty promises

00:09:00.305 --> 00:09:02.641
came crashing down on the
workers he promised to help,

00:09:02.641 --> 00:09:04.977
all Trump could do
was offer a useless tweet.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.845
And, once again,
he clearly had no idea how

00:09:06.845 --> 00:09:08.347
to deliver on his promise.

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:10.883
-"Just spoke to Mary Barra,
CEO of General Motors,

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:12.818
about the Lordstown,
Ohio, plant.

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:15.353
I am not happy that it is closed

00:09:15.353 --> 00:09:17.623
when everything else
in our country is booming.

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:20.492
I asked her to sell it
or do something quickly.

00:09:20.492 --> 00:09:23.328
She blamed the UAW union.

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:25.997
I don't care.
I just want it open.

00:09:25.997 --> 00:09:28.700
-Hey, ass[bleep], you told them
not to sell their homes.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.404
A tweet whining that you're not
happy isn't good enough.

00:09:31.404 --> 00:09:33.505
It's like if your buddy told you
to invest everything you have

00:09:33.505 --> 00:09:35.808
in Bitcoin and, then,
when it crashed, sent you a text

00:09:35.808 --> 00:09:37.943
that was just a dollar emoji
and a surprise face.

00:09:37.943 --> 00:09:38.944
[ Laughter and clapping ]

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:40.079
Also, what do you mean,

00:09:40.079 --> 00:09:41.580
"I asked her to do something"?

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.449
Do what?
You're the guy

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:45.417
who said you were gonna
save the jobs.

00:09:45.417 --> 00:09:47.252
You're supposed
to have the ideas.

00:09:47.252 --> 00:09:50.289
Like a plumber who shows up
and takes a look at your toilet,

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:52.925
and then just screams, "Unclog!"

00:09:52.925 --> 00:09:55.594
[ Laughter ]

00:09:55.594 --> 00:09:57.263
[ Applause ]

00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:59.731
By the way, that plant
in Ohio is far from alone.

00:09:59.731 --> 00:10:02.267
In fact, just two weeks ago,
GM idled another plant

00:10:02.267 --> 00:10:04.403
in Michigan,
which might come as a shock

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:06.171
to people who were
at these Trump rallies

00:10:06.171 --> 00:10:08.540
in Michigan in 2016.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.676
-I've been saying:
Your car industry's

00:10:10.676 --> 00:10:12.077
being sucked
away from Michigan.

00:10:12.077 --> 00:10:13.278
It's happening.

00:10:13.278 --> 00:10:17.282
If I'm elected,
you won't lose one plant.

00:10:17.282 --> 00:10:19.284
You'll have plants coming
into this country.

00:10:19.284 --> 00:10:20.919
You're gonna have jobs again.

00:10:20.919 --> 00:10:21.987
You won't lose one plant.

00:10:21.987 --> 00:10:23.121
I promise you that.

00:10:23.221 --> 00:10:24.690
[ Cheering and applause ]
I promise you that.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:27.459
So all I say is this:
You wanna build your plant

00:10:27.459 --> 00:10:29.428
in Mexico,
have a great time.

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:31.329
But if you think you're
gonna ship your product

00:10:31.329 --> 00:10:33.165
across the border -- which will
be a very strong border,

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:35.401
by the way --
for no tax, no nothing.

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:37.169
So we end up with unemployment

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:40.305
and we end up with empty
plants and factories.

00:10:40.305 --> 00:10:43.976
And you end up with the money,
the jobs, and the plants.

00:10:43.976 --> 00:10:45.177
You can forget it.

00:10:45.177 --> 00:10:46.745
And you know what would happen?

00:10:46.745 --> 00:10:49.348
If you said that right upfront,
nobody's leaving, folks.

00:10:49.348 --> 00:10:50.549
You stop it right away.

00:10:50.549 --> 00:10:53.285
The politicians
don't wanna say that

00:10:53.285 --> 00:10:56.421
because most of them are too
stupid to even understand it.

00:10:56.421 --> 00:10:57.890
-They're too stupid?

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:01.226
Dude, you're too stupid
to spell the word country,

00:11:01.226 --> 00:11:03.328
your wife's name,
and your own name.

00:11:03.328 --> 00:11:05.364
[ Laughter and applause ]
I mean,

00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:07.466
imagine if this guy

00:11:07.466 --> 00:11:09.902
tried meeting his own
immigration standards.

00:11:09.902 --> 00:11:12.604
He has no discernible skills,
lost $1 billion,

00:11:12.604 --> 00:11:13.838
and can't spell his own name.

00:11:13.838 --> 00:11:15.440
He'd flunk
the citizenship test

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.042
before he even got
to the first question.

00:11:17.042 --> 00:11:19.011
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:21.881
Trump inflicts cruelty
on desperate migrants

00:11:21.881 --> 00:11:24.549
fleeing poverty and violence
because, first, he's a racist

00:11:24.549 --> 00:11:26.351
and racism is at the core
of his ideology.

00:11:26.351 --> 00:11:29.154
And second, he's failed
at literally everything else

00:11:29.154 --> 00:11:30.255
he's promised to do.

00:11:30.255 --> 00:11:32.958
You need a plan
to expand healthcare,

00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:34.259
save manufacturing jobs.

00:11:34.259 --> 00:11:36.361
You can't just do it
by tweeting

00:11:36.361 --> 00:11:38.163
or yelling at people,
but Trump is...

00:11:38.163 --> 00:11:40.265
-Too stupid to even
understand it.

00:11:40.265 --> 00:11:41.266
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:41.266 --> 00:11:45.104
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

